  "question": {
    "text": "Let two points be <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mtext>'</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mtext>'</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math> be such that the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units and it lies on the line&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then a value of <math><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is"
  },
